(text "No fuse / TVS / switch: cost-down decision.\nTypical draw ≈ 10 mA, max 21 mA @ 5 V.\nTP1–TP3, TP5, TP6: bare pads on the back for the pogo-pin SWD jig." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 157.48 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "93251402-c5f5-517b-a921-df787d1eb5ec"))
(text "DRIVE SCHEME\nScan by anode: phase p (0..15) drives line Lp HIGH, the cathodes of LEDs lit in that phase LOW,\nall other lines Hi-Z. 16 phases per frame, binary-code-modulated PWM (8 bit, 2 µs slot, 122 Hz).\nLED Dn+1 sits at board position n (reading order, top->bottom, left->right). Which anode/cathode pair sits at\nwhich position is chosen by scripts/optimize_leds.py (hardware/led_assignment.json): neighbouring LED pads\nshare line nets, so each net is a few copper islands joined by tiny bridges and the board routes on 2 layers.\n\nTOUCH STAR\nThe star is one electrode on BOTH copper layers, joined by a plated hole. PA7 samples it with\nADC charge sharing: hover < light touch < firm press < squeeze (pinched front + back = biggest signal).\n\nPRODUCTION\nPY32F003F18P6 = TSSOP-20 'pinout 1' (datasheet fig. 3-3). SWD via pogo pads TP3 (SWDIO), TP5 (SWCLK),\nTP6 (NRST), connect-under-reset; after boot the firmware takes PA13/PA14 over as lines L8/L9." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 269.24 22.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "34f2662d-409a-5968-8f67-4c4348ecb69f"))
(rectangle (start 266.7 20.32) (end 406.4 124.46) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "7230f3a3-bf06-5cb3-8d0f-e0ad2ad18658"))
(text "LED MATRIX  —  240 × XL-1608WWC-06 warm white 0603, charlieplexed on 16 lines" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 129.54 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3ba33b30-e721-51c5-804a-1975d31ac589"))
(rectangle (start 17.78 127) (end 271.78 281.94) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "ca653246-958a-5eb8-aafa-12a544f3fbef"))
(text "HOW TO READ THE MATRIX\n\nEach row is one charlieplex line driving the ANODES\n(bus wire, line name on the left end of the bus).\n\nEach LED's CATHODE goes to the line named\njust left of it.\n\nReference Dn = board position n-1 in reading order\n(top -> bottom, left -> right), see the notes above.\n\nL0..L15 connect to R1..R16 in the MCU block." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 279.4 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2880e8f0-5137-5c61-b877-8b04970d2f67"))
(rectangle (start 276.86 127) (end 406.4 205.74) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "8834a552-bfac-556e-870f-8fbf2923eb77"))
